5. Live residuals (named, not “missing symbol”)
---

### R-bc — `emit-bc` skip-check
`main.oo` `emit-bc` does **not** call `run_check_core` /
`check_secret_println_sinks`. tmp `stmt_fail` → `CALL println 1` rc=0.
`run` still refuses (check first). Same class as s28 R-bc-secret.

### R-cache — repo-cwd false OK
`check_mod.oo` writes `.ooda-cache/check/<hash>` = `OK\n`. First
`oodac check fixtures/secret_sink_fail.oo` from workspace hit
`/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/.ooda-cache` and printed **OK** rc=0.
Clean `/tmp` cwd: rc=1 `ERR\tsecret`. s71 R9. Auditors must not
prove check from a dirty cache tree.

### R-print / R-log — skip-check emit
| Shape | emit-c | check | emit-llvm |
|-------|--------|-------|-----------|
| `print(SECRET)` | rc=0 `oo_print_str` (llvm builtin `print`) | type `undefined variable 'print'` | rc=0 `@oo_print_str` (s3cret in IR) |
| `log(SECRET)` | rc=1 `log sink refuses SECRET` (**guard**) | type `undefined 'log'` | rc=0 `call @log` (check walker has no `log`) |

`print` is an LLVM-only println **shape** (s71 R2). Not a typed product
API. C emit of `print(...)` is an unresolved call, not `oo_print_*`.

### R-1char-let — `let <1-char> = println(SECRET)`
Not product stmt form. Repro (clean cwd, cache wiped):

| dest | check | emit-c |
|------|-------|--------|
| `r` `x` `y` `z` `a` `b` `c` | **OK** rc=0 | **abort** rc=134 `malloc(): unaligned tcache chunk detected` |
| `tmp` `rr` `r1` `_x` `dest` | rc=1 `… SECRET api_key` | (check dies first) |

Same OK+abort for `let r = eprintln(SECRET)`. Tokens of the fail-open
shape are ordinary (`IDENT println` / `LPAREN` / `IDENT api_key`).
Likely `c_env` 1-char dest vs 1-char kind (`S`/`I`/`T`/`R`/`F`) —
**not** a missing symbol. Stmt `println(SECRET)` after `let api_key = …`
still refuses.

### R-host-stale
Same 07:49 ELF as s28/s61/s71/s72/s710. Source newer (7.10/2.10/6.1
order). Do not nm a post-2.9-unify ELF; none exists.

